<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · war</p><h1 class="enc-title">Soviet–Afghan War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1979">1979</a>–<a href="/years/1989">1989</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Soviet war in Afghanistan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Soviet–Afghan War was fought in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a> from December 1979 to February 1989 between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a> and the Afghan Armed Forces and the Afghan mujahideen, whose external support came mostly from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, the United Kingdom, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> and the Arab states of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persian-gulf">Persian Gulf</a>. Soviet troops held the major cities while the mujahideen fought a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guerrilla-warfare">guerrilla</a> war in the countryside, and the Soviets laid millions of landmines and levelled villages. Between one and three million <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghans">Afghans</a> died. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mikhail-gorbachev">Mikhail Gorbachev</a> the Soviet army withdrew, its last column leaving on 15 February 1989.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/soviet-afghan-war.jpg" alt="Soviet–Afghan War" width="330" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: erwinlux · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mortar_attack_on_Shigal_Tarna_garrison,_Kunar_Province,_87.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
